==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{suffix|en|Switzer|-land}}, adopted in the 16th century from Early Modern {{der|en|de|Schwytzerland|t=land of the Swiss}}. Noun sense refers to the state’s political neutrality in both World Wars.

{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈswɪt.sə.lənd/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈswɪt.sɚ.lənd/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Switzerland.ogg|a=US}}

